schema: public-use-boundary
object:
  title: Boundary — Regen Coordination 2024 funding-distribution figures
  tier: public-with-caveat
  consent_note: >-
    Covers the claim-evidence entry "Regen Coordination distributed
    $236,000+ to communities across 2024" (same work order). The underlying
    figures are from a public ReFi DAO blog wrap-up, but funding-distribution
    data is treated as high-risk by default per framework policy; verify
    figures against the source post before reusing them in external comms or
    grant reporting.
  review_type: steward-review-before-external-comms-use
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/first-90-days.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: |
    # assessed-but-excluded
    - Named-individual quote from Tereza Bízková (ReFi Medellín co-founder) —
      kept as attributed quoted text inside the track/claim-evidence/
      encyclopedia-entry fields (she is already a public, named source in a
      published interview); no standalone public person-node created.
    - "Try This" action prompts — coaching/exercise content, not extracted as
      a separate knowledge object.
    - Liberating Structures (specific facilitation formats like 1-2-4-All,
      Troika Consulting) — considered for its own concept-lineage entry but
      folded into the track's `concepts` list instead, since the article
      treats it as a supporting method rather than a concept central to this
      source the way local-node and quadratic-funding are.
